        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "not impose it on others. We should strive for a style that is no simpler than our ideas require but also no more difficult than it has to be.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                117,
                770,
                166
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    166.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    166.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This ideal is an ethical one and can be expressed in what we'll call the \"golden rule\" of style:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                169,
                771,
                220
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    169.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    169.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    220.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    220.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Write to others as you would have others write to you.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                232,
                581,
                256
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    114.0,
                    232.0
                ],
                [
                    581.0,
                    232.0
                ],
                [
                    581.0,
                    256.0
                ],
                [
                    114.0,
                    256.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We write most ethically when we would trade places with our intended readers and experience the consequences they do after they read our writing. Unfortunately, writers don't or can't always live up to that altruistic ideal. Some simply fall short; some give precedence to other values; some by choice or obligation favor other interests over those of their readers. It is up to us as readers to distinguish these circumstances and then to make ethical judgments.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                270,
                772,
                426
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    270.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    270.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    426.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    426.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Clarity and Other Values",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                455,
                396,
                486
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    455.0
                ],
                [
                    396.0,
                    455.0
                ],
                [
                    396.0,
                    486.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    486.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "How should we judge writers who violate the golden rule of style because they favor some other value over their readers' interests? We began our first lesson by saying that correctness is an important good but not the highest one. We ended that lesson by showing you how to write in a gender-inclusive fashion while still writing \"correctly\" (see pp. 16–21). The issue is one of competing values. Here are three instances for you to consider.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                500,
                772,
                654
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    500.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    500.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    654.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    654.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Is it unethical for writers to persist in using gendered nouns such as comedienne or policeman when gender-inclusive alternatives such as comic or police officer are ready at hand? We could say that it is. By deliberately choosing not to use these alternatives, such writers risk violating our golden rule, for it is certainly plausible that some writers would object to having their genders gratuitously noted or ignored if they were in their readers' shoes. And it is hard to imagine what other value or commitment is at stake, other than a nostalgia for traditional gender roles.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                656,
                772,
                836
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    656.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    656.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    836.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    836.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This case is slightly more complicated: what about writers who avoid using they with indefinite referents out of an allegiance to “correct” usage?",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                838,
                771,
                888
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    838.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    838.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    888.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    888.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Anyone who wants a driver's license must have their eyes examined.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                901,
                653,
                924
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
